533 0 obj
<<
/Title (DiabetSavior is a digital health management app that I worked on with my team for the Google Solution Challenge 2023. The idea came from the challenges we identified in the daily routines of people with diabetes, particularly remembering medication schedules, monitoring blood glucose, and managing other parts of their treatment routine. As a Hipster \(UI/UX Designer\), I worked on mapping the user journey, designing the app flows and interfaces in Figma, and creating a component-based design system. I also designed different flows based on the needs of Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes users and worked closely with our Flutter developer to make sure the designs could be implemented properly. Our biggest challenge was presenting complex health-related information in a way that was still easy to understand. To address this, we used step-by-step flows, confirmations for important actions, and clear visual indicators to help reduce the chance of users misunderstanding the information. The project was successfully submitted to the Google Solution Challenge 2023. Through this experience, I learned that designing a digital product, especially one related to healthcare, is not only about creating an appealing interface, but also about making users feel safe, confident, and supported when using it.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 382 0 R
>>
endobj
