657 0 obj
<<
/Title (YoloVision is an assistive AI wearable and software application designed to empower visually impaired individuals with independent spatial awareness, supporting UN SDG 10 \(Reduced Inequalities\). By combining YOLOv11 for real-time object detection, OCR for reading printed text, and Text-to-Speech \(TTS\), the system converts surrounding scenes and printed information into immediate audio feedback. The idea came from our observation that visually impaired individuals may still rely on others for everyday activities such as navigating unfamiliar surroundings, recognizing objects, and reading text. In this group project, I contributed to the problem formulation process, synthesized accessibility requirements, designed low-cognitive-load user flows and the 3D wearable interface concept, and pitched the working prototype at the innovation exhibition. One of our main challenges was avoiding cognitive overload when the AI detected multiple objects at once. We addressed this by prioritizing nearby objects and delivering the information through bone-conduction audio, allowing users to receive feedback while remaining aware of sounds in their surroundings. This project taught me about multimodal accessibility design, audio UX feedback principles, and how to bridge AI engineering with human-centered design. YoloVision also received 4th place in the innovation competition.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
